<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yoweri Museveni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yoweri Museveni is a Ugandan politician and former rebel leader who has been President of Uganda since 1986. Born in Ankole, he fought against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idi-amin">Idi Amin</a> and then led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-resistance-army">National Resistance Army</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ugandan-bush-war">Ugandan Bush War</a>, which brought him to power. He restored the traditional kingdoms as cultural institutions in 1993, and constitutional changes removed term and age limits on his presidency.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yoweri-museveni.jpg" alt="Yoweri Museveni" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DFID - UK Department for International Development · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Museveni_July_2012_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The region has also produced many national figures, including President <b>Yoweri Museveni</b>, who was born in Ankole.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-ankole">Kingdom of Ankole · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Under President <b>Yoweri Museveni</b> the monarchy was restored as a cultural institution, and Ronald Muwenda Mutebi II was crowned in 1993.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-buganda">Kingdom of Buganda · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>From 1987 <b>Yoweri Museveni</b>’s government adopted reforms backed by the International Monetary Fund, liberalised the coffee trade and invited expelled Asians to reclaim their property, and Uganda achieved some of the fastest growth in Africa during the 1990s.</blockquote><a href="/empire/uganda">Uganda · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Ntungamo, in what is now <a href="/countries/uganda">Uganda</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=-0.88,30.27&amp;year=1979" aria-label="Ntungamo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5391 2197 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Yoweri Museveni"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5841 2467h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5841 2467h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=-0.88,30.27&amp;year=1979">What was here in 1979? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
